<title>USA: Edison sees scattered outages from winds.</title>
<headline>Edison sees scattered outages from winds.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strong winds led to power outages for as many as 75,000 customers within Southern California Edison's service territory since Sunday night, a utility spokesman said Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are having some sporadic service interruptions throughout Southern California. Some lines have come back up, but others have gone down,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The spokesman noted most of the outages are at the distribution level and no high-voltage lines have been affected.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
</text>
